1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,590
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,910
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:05,980
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,810
I've been welding in a
shipyard

5
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,090
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:11,160
Kneeling and crouching on
steel decks,

7
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,370
all day long.

8
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,650
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:15,290
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,670
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,270
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,570
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:21,690
and it went away.

14
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:22,970
This is different.

15
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:23,490
Tight.

16
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:24,240
Full.

17
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,150
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,660
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:27,620
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:28,900
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,130
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,990
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:34,450
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:35,490
At three months,

25
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:36,690
give it six.

26
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:37,960
At six months,

27
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,760
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,920
At a year,

29
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,760
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:44,590
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,170
We went down the list.

32
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:47,850
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:49,150
Every session,

34
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:50,830
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,300
I got stronger.

36
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:53,980
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:55,480
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,800
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:56,970 --> 00:00:59,210
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:00,250
and nobody could tell me

41
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,560
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:02,890
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:05,550
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,110
And after that, a second
operation

45
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:08,700
to go back

46
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,230
in and do it over.

47
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:11,510
I said no.

48
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:13,330
Every morning I climbed
down

49
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:14,600
into the dry dock

50
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:15,670
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:17,720
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:20,140
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,070
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:23,580
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,250
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,470
couldn't stand at the
counter

57
00:01:26,470 --> 00:01:28,040
long enough to finish
dinner,

58
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,850
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

59
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:31,660
without shifting every two
minutes.

60
00:01:31,770 --> 00:01:33,820
The guys on my crew
started taking

61
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:35,010
the low welds for me.

62
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,430
Thirty years,

63
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:37,830
and I started wondering

64
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:38,830
how many more ships I

65
00:01:38,830 --> 00:01:39,870
had left in me.

66
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,370
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:42,840
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,060
like getting in the car

69
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:45,250
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:46,240
into a decision.

71
00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:47,770
After a long and serious

72
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:49,150
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,950
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,920
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,610
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,200
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,110
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,040
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,020
nothing wrong.

80
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,430
Only this time

81
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:02,690
there was no new number.

82
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,960
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,660
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:07,650
I sat in the parking

85
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:08,480
lot for a while.

86
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,720
Okay, I thought.

87
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:11,050
Then explain this.

88
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,400
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

89
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,840
I hit my breaking point.

90
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:16,760
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

91
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:17,570
I had a hull

92
00:02:17,570 --> 00:02:18,980
to start on at six.

93
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:21,270
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:21,270 --> 00:02:23,150
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:24,370
with my leg up,

96
00:02:24,370 --> 00:02:26,080
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,340
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:28,990
was wrapped around my knee

99
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:29,960
and tightening.

100
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,640
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,440
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:35,090 --> 00:02:35,960
And I just thought,

103
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,530
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:39,020
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:41,040
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:41,870
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,470
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:44,820
And when I found one,

109
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:46,070
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:47,630
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:48,070 --> 00:02:49,270
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:50,550
out and went looking.

113
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:51,890
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,930 --> 00:02:53,200
For an explanation.

115
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,180
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:57,250
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:57,250 --> 00:03:00,000
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:01,520
And that's when I found a
video

119
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,310
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

120
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,730
Steven Salinger,

121
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:06,170
whose own wife had been

122
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:07,500
through exactly this.

123
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,480
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,100
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,250
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:13,290 --> 00:03:14,200
The ice.

127
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,930
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,660
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:17,750 --> 00:03:18,920
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:21,180
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:22,680
Fast relief

132
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,570
isn't relief.

133
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:24,670
It's a preview.

134
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,170
So I'm not going to tell

135
00:03:26,170 --> 00:03:27,510
you this works fast.

136
00:03:27,550 --> 00:03:28,400
It doesn't.

137
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:30,450
But if you're willing to
be patient,

138
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:31,110
and to look at what's

139
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,410
going on around your new
knee

140
00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:33,880
instead of inside it,
there

141
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,850
is a real reason it still
hurts.

142
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,760
And something you can do
about it.

143
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:39,500
Let me explain what he
said,

144
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,690
because this is what
changed

145
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:41,720
everything for me.

146
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,560
He started with the
basics.

147
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,190
A knee replacement takes
out

148
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:46,950
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

149
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:48,210
in metal and plastic.

150
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:50,180
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

151
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,770
you had before the
operation.

152
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,640
That part I already knew.

153
00:03:53,810 --> 00:03:55,130
But then he explained
something

154
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:56,570
nobody had ever told me.

155
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,170
He said,

156
00:03:57,170 --> 00:03:58,460
think about a swollen foot

157
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,430
inside a shoe.

158
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:00,970
The shoe didn't shrink.

159
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:03,250
Your foot is taking up
more room,

160
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:04,770
so everything feels
cramped

161
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:06,350
and tight and squeezed.

162
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,810
Your new knee sits

163
00:04:07,810 --> 00:04:09,420
in a limited space with
living

164
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,260
tissue packed all around
it.

165
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:13,120
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

166
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,640
had to work through that
tissue.

167
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:17,000
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

168
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:18,600
At first that's normal.

169
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,050
But in some people

170
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:21,550
that swelling can stay
switched

171
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:23,530
on far longer than
expected.

172
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,330
And swollen tissue takes
up more

173
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:27,050
room than calm tissue
does.

174
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,790
So when you bend,

175
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:30,530
that tissue gets
compressed.

176
00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:31,700
When you straighten,

177
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:33,080
it gets pulled tight.

178
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,430
That's the band.

179
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:36,530
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

180
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:37,540
And you start being

181
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:38,590
the one who says,

182
00:04:38,590 --> 00:04:39,950
you guys go ahead.

183
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:41,190
I'll stay here.

184
00:04:41,330 --> 00:04:42,980
And that's exactly why so
much

185
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:45,090
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

186
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,240
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

187
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,150
around the knee.

188
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:49,210
Worth doing,

189
00:04:49,210 --> 00:04:50,070
and I'd done it.

190
00:04:50,110 --> 00:04:51,420
It does nothing about
tissue

191
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,450
taking up room.

192
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:53,740
A nerve block quiets

193
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:55,290
the nerve carrying the
signal.

194
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,790
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

195
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,680
But when that irritated
tissue

196
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,220
finally calms down,

197
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:02,700
it holds less fluid,

198
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:04,310
and it takes up less room.

199
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,340
Less room taken up means

200
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,310
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

201
00:05:08,710 --> 00:05:10,360
That's what takes the
pressure off.

202
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:12,190
After two years of this,

203
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,760
it finally made sense.

204
00:05:14,090 --> 00:05:15,980
The problem was never the
new knee.

205
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:18,020
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

206
00:05:18,350 --> 00:05:19,870
He calls it the squeeze.

207
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:22,370
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

208
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,480
I'd bought knee sleeves,

209
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,050
welding knee pads,

210
00:05:26,050 --> 00:05:28,750
compression braces,
creams,

211
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,540
half of Amazon really,

212
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:31,780
and all any of it gave

213
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:32,820
me was an hour.

214
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,980
I even looked at going

215
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,950
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

216
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,960
But at $200 a session

217
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,770
with nothing covered by
insurance,

218
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:41,310
that was a quick no.

219
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:43,120
Then one night I went back

220
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,830
to that knee replacement
group

221
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:45,980
and actually read it.

222
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,600
Thousands of people,

223
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,170
years out from surgery,

224
00:05:49,170 --> 00:05:51,560
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

225
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,000
nobody could explain.

226
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,510
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

227
00:05:55,510 --> 00:05:57,460
the same thing kept coming
up.

228
00:05:57,620 --> 00:05:59,400
This one device,

229
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,970
and people saying it was
the first

230
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:02,470
thing that made a
difference.

231
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:04,610
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

232
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:05,790
alright, here it comes,

233
00:06:05,790 --> 00:06:07,190
he's selling me something,

234
00:06:07,190 --> 00:06:08,990
let me shut that down
right now.

235
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:11,170
I'm only here because I
made myself

236
00:06:11,170 --> 00:06:13,390
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

237
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:14,310
that if I ever found

238
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:15,460
something that helped,

239
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,510
I'd say so.

240
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:18,070
It's called the KenRelief

241
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,620
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

242
00:06:19,910 --> 00:06:22,050
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

243
00:06:22,330 --> 00:06:24,050
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

244
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:26,300
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

245
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:29,070
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:29,070 --> 00:06:29,970
just to see what all

247
00:06:29,970 --> 00:06:31,100
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,230
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

249
00:06:34,230 --> 00:06:36,990
charge $200 a session

250
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:38,360
for, off machines that
cost

251
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,150
fifty thousand dollars,

252
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,160
in a wrap you plug

253
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,380
into the wall at home.

254
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:44,580
Two hundred and forty
lights.

255
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,060
Red at 660 nanometers

256
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:49,300
and near-infrared at 850,

257
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,340
run together for the
strongest effect.

258
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:52,640
Four strength levels.

259
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:54,540
A five to thirty minute
timer.

260
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,000
Then I saw the guarantee.

261
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,150
Ninety days.

262
00:06:57,350 --> 00:06:59,840
Results or your money
back,

263
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,120
no questions,

264
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,500
no store credit,

265
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:04,710
and you don't even send it
back.

266
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:07,210
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

267
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:08,800
days to change my mind.

268
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,680
There wasn't much to lose,

269
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,860
so I ordered it.

270
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,150
Two of them, actually.

271
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:15,700
Only the right knee was
replaced,

272
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,950
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

273
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:19,550
and I'd done it for two
years.

274
00:07:19,590 --> 00:07:21,560
The left one was carrying
the difference.

275
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:22,590
When it came,

276
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:24,800
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

277
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,950
because I'd been let down
too

278
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:27,450
many times to get excited.

279
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:30,090
What I felt was warmth.

280
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,320
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

281
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:34,380
More like it was coming
from inside

282
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:36,280
the knee and spreading
around it.

283
